    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present 'Coral Lodge', a truly exceptional Tudor-inspired four-bedroom detached residence, set on a private and mature approx. 0.62-acre site in an exclusive enclave of just four homes. Located on a quiet avenue just minutes' walk from Loughshinny Crossroads, the beautiful sandy beach, and the picturesque harbour, this home offers an ideal blend of countryside tranquillity and coastal charm.\n\nExtending to approx. 240 sq.m., Coral Lodge comes to the market in wonderful condition. Designed and finished to a high specification, and well maintained throughout, this substantial property offers an outstanding opportunity for families seeking space, versatility, and a peaceful setting within easy reach of all amenities.\nThe extensive gardens are a true highlight of the property, featuring manicured lawns, mature trees, a large patio area perfect for entertaining, a greenhouse, and a charming children's playhouse.\n\nAccessed via electric gates, a sweeping tarmac driveway leads to the rear of the home and provides ample parking.\n\nIn addition, the property boasts a range of outbuildings that significantly enhance its appeal and versatility:\n\nLarge industrial shed, ideal for a wide range of uses including as a workshop, builder's yard, mechanic's garage, or for a small business\n\nDetached block-built workshop, fully plumbed and wired, currently housing a sauna, and suitable for use as a home gym or studio\n\nA further block-built unit offering excellent potential to be converted into a self-contained one-bedroom unit, subject to the necessary planning permission\n\nSet within Ballykea, this idyllic property enjoys a prime location in the heart of Loughshinny, a peaceful seaside village in North County Dublin. Just minutes from the thriving coastal town of Skerries, residents can enjoy a wide selection of restaurants, cafés, boutiques, and a commuter railway station.\n\nThe area is well-served by an abundance of recreational and sporting facilities, including golf, sailing, rugby, soccer, GAA, and tennis clubs. Excellent public transport links, with the bus stop within minutes walk of the property, along with easy access to the M1, M50, and Dublin Airport, make commuting simple and convenient."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - \nTiled floor, vaulted wooden ceiling\n\nHallway - \nTiled floor, cloakroom, under stairs storage\n\nLiving Room - \nWood floor, bright spacious room, feature fireplace with multi fuel stove, recessed lights, bay window\n\nFamily Room - \nWood floor, bay window with built in seating, wall to wall storage unit\n\nHome Office - \nWood floor, wood panelled ceiling, built in desk, recessed lights\n\nSunroom - \nWood floor, wood panelled ceiling, wall panelling, French doors to patio area\n\nBathroom - \nFully tiled walls and floor, WC, WHB vanity unit, shower unit, fan, window\n\nKitchen Dining Room - \nTiled floor, fitted kitchen with wall and floor mounted units, tiled splash back, velux window, French doors to front garden\n\nUtility Room - \nTiled floor, fitted presses, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, door to rear garden\n\nLanding - \nWood floor, spacious area, stira to attic, eaves storage, feature window\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor, part tiled walls, WC, WHB, bath with fully tiled walls, velux window\n\nMain Bedroom - \nWood floor, large double bedroom, access to private balcony area over looking rear garden, eaves storage\n\nEn-suite - \nTiled floor, WC, WHB vanity unit with tiled splash back, shower unit with fully tiled walls, velux window\n\nBedroom 2 - \nWood floor, spacious double room, built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - \nCarpet to floor, spacious double room, built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 4 - \nCarpet to floor, spacious double room, built in wardrobes\n\nGardens - \nIndustrial shed: alarmed, electrics, 100 sq.m.Block Built Shed: Electrics, sauna, previously in use as a stableBlock built Unit: Potential as a one bedroom separate unit subject to the necessary planning permissionGlasshouse, patio areas, manicured lawns, mature trees with a varity of apple trees\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Stunning Tudor-style detached home on approx. 0.62 acres</li><li> Four spacious bedrooms, main with en-suite</li><li> O.F.C.H.</li><li> Multiple reception rooms and home office</li><li> Large industrial shed ideal for business or workshop use</li><li> Detached workshop with sauna ideal for gym/studio</li><li> Additional outbuilding with potential for one-bed unit (SPP)</li><li> Electric gated entrance and sweeping driveway</li><li> Landscaped gardens with patio, greenhouse & playhouse</li><li> Minutes to Loughshinny beach and close to Skerries town</li><li> Excellent transport links & local amenities</ul>"
      },
